# Sparse runoff package parameters (pkg/rnf)
#
# The same runoff as the dense case input.rnof_clim, in sparse form:
# 12 records of 2628000 s from 16 January 1978 12:00,
# repeating: mitgcm_time_sampling = "fixed" with
# mitgcm_time_repeat = "annual". The repeat cycle is the
# span of time_bnds (365 days) and it is anchored on the
# real date of record 1, as exf's runoffRepCycle is.
#
# The file is written by ../input.rnof_const/gen_sparse.py from the
# dense records of input.rnof_clim and is read from that directory,
# so both cases force the model with the same runoff. Every timing
# value the reader needs comes from the file's own time axis, which is
# what this case checks; data.rnf overrides nothing.
 &RNF_PARM01
  RNF_file = '../input.rnof_clim/runoff_sparse.nc',
 &
